      "body": "## Motivation\n\nCloses #43931.\n\n`SGLANG_NGRAM_FORCE_GREEDY_VERIFY` is still registered in `environ.py` and referenced from the speculative decoding docs, but nothing consumes it anymore. NGRAM verify read the flag in `ngram_info.py` back in #13153; the read was lost when NGRAM verify moved onto the shared `eagle_sample()` helper, so setting the env var today has no effect.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `eagle_sample()` gains a keyword-only `force_greedy_verify` (default `False`); when set, the greedy predicate treats the batch as all-greedy.\n- The NGRAM call site passes `envs.SGLANG_NGRAM_FORCE_GREEDY_VERIFY.get()`. EAGLE and the other callers keep the default, so their acceptance behavior is unchanged.\n- New unit test `test_ngram_force_greedy_verify.py` pins the plumbing at the predicate seam: flag on forces the greedy branch for a mixed batch, flag off preserves batch semantics, an already all-greedy batch is unaffected either way.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nDefault-path behavior is unchanged when the flag is unset; with the flag set, NGRAM verify selects the existing greedy branch instead of the sampling one. No GPU on this machine, so I ran the new unit test on CPU (3 passed) and left end-to-end output comparison to CI.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A: one env lookup per NGRAM verify call, no kernel or hot-path changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (ruff check with the repo's selected rules + ruff format)\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (not needed: the docs already describe the flag, this change makes the code match them)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (N/A, see above)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38487314015](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38487314015)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38487313954](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38487313954)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38487314038](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38487314038)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
